old tolerant cantaloupe melon cultivar well suited for duller UK summer weather. Best grown in a greenhouse, but may be planted under cloches or even in the open under fleece. It produces yellow-green netter fruit with aromatic, sweet orange flesh","image":"","commonName":"melon 'Emir'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":199931,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>melo</em> 'Galia'","entityDescription":"A vigorous greenhouse melon cultivar producing round, yellow fruit with attractive ‘netting’ and sweet, pale green to creamy white flesh. Shows resistance to powdery mildews","image":"visi169083.jpg","commonName":"melon 'Galia'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":518185,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>melo</em> 'Honey Bun'","entityDescription":"A compact, bushy variety of melon, grey-green on the outside with dark orange flesh and a sweet flavour.  Each plant is capable of producing up to 4 fruits if growing conditions are favourable","image":"","commonName":"melon 'Honey Bun'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":112426,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>melo</em> 'Ogen'","entityDescription":"A cantaloupe type greenhouse melon cultivar. It produces smaller, round, greenish yellow fruit with distinct stripes up 15cm in diameter. The flesh is pale green and very sweet","image":"","commonName":"melon 'Ogen'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":297286,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>melo</em> 'Pepito'","entityDescription":"A cantaloupe type, greenhouse melon cultivar producing oval ‘rugby ball’ shaped fruit with deep orange, sweet flesh. Shows good disease resistance","image":"","commonName":"melon 'Pepito'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":158213,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>metuliferus</em> (F)","entityDescription":"A climbing or scrambling annual which reaches 2.5m. It has green lobed leaves and yellow flowers. These develop into horned fruit the size of an egg, which ripen to a golden yellow. The flesh and pips inside are green","image":"moja03429.jpg","commonName":"African horned cucumber","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":105568,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>sativus</em>","entityDescription":"The wild species of cucumber from which all other cultivars have been derived. It is a deciduous, annual, vining plant to 2m (6½ft) high, climbing by means of thin tendrils at the leaf nodes and producing yellow separate male and female flowers on the same plant the females after pollination, bearing the familiar, cylindrical, dark green, edible fruit, up to 40cm (16in) in length","image":"visi168668.jpg","commonName":"cucumber","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":378140,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>sativus</em> 'Amadora'","entityDescription":"A perennial trailing or climbing plant usually grown as an annual.  This compact, high-yielding, female only variety is suited to indoor growing, producing yellow flowers followed by mini snack cucumbers on small vines which are crunchy, seedless and with no need to peel.  Suitable for smaller spaces","image":"","commonName":"cucumber 'Amadora'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":173930,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>sativus</em> 'Burpless Tasty Green'","entityDescription":"A vining deciduous annual to 3m (10ft) high producing dark green, easily digestible crisp and flavourful fruits, to 25cm (10in) long in summer. It is a ridge variety so named because of its warty skin and which is more suitable to growing outdoors in summer in the UK climate, than the more warmth-loving greenhouse varieties. All ridge varieties need to be pollinated to produce fruit, so the male flowers should not be removed.","image":"","commonName":"cucumber (ridge) 'Burpless Tasty Green'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":119336,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>sativus</em> 'Bush Champion'","entityDescription":"A non-climbing deciduous annual plant, which as its name suggests, produces compact, bushy plants to 25cm (10in) high and 90cm (3ft) across. It is a prolific and early fruiting variety, producing 25-30cm (19-12in) long cucumbers, which are crisp and well flavoured. Its short, compact habit, make it ideal for growing in containers on the patio, or where space is limited.","image":"","commonName":"cucumber 'Bush Champion' (ridge)","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":139319,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>sativus</em> 'Carmen'","entityDescription":"A high-yielding cucumber with good disease-resistance. 40cm long, straight, mild-flavoured fruits are produced on climbing plants from late summer into autumn. Best grown under glass","image":"CucumberCarmen.jpg","commonName":"cucumber 'Carmen'","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":173948,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>sativus</em> 'Crystal Apple'","entityDescription":"An unusual heritage variety, producing climbing plants up to 3m (10ft) high and producing round, golf-ball sized fruit, which have randomly spaced, short black bristles over their skins. The cucmbers are sweet and juicy and are ready to harvest when they turn from green to lemon-yellow. It is suitable for growing outdoors in the UK in a sheltered spot in full sun.","image":"grjo02386.jpg","commonName":"cucumber 'Crystal Apple'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":173947,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>sativus</em> 'Crystal Lemon'","entityDescription":"A vigorous climbing cucumber suitable for growing outdoors or under glass. Leaves are mid-green and lobed, and yellow flowers are followed by round, yellow fruit from midsummer to early autumn","image":"RHS-0001969.jpg","commonName":"cucumber 'Crystal Lemon'","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":293191,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>sativus</em> 'Cucino'","entityDescription":"A vigorous cucumber cultivar up to 3m tall producing heavy crops of small, crisp, 'snack-size' mini-fruits from summer into autumn","image":"","commonName":"cucumber 'Cucino'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":388146,"botanicalName":"<em>Cucumis</em> <em>sativus</em> 'Delistar'","entityDescription":"A perennial trailing or climbing plant usually grown as an annual.  This variety is suited to indoor growing in pots and containers, producing yellow flowers followed by small, aromatic, sweet and crunchy fruit around 16-18cm in length, with thin skins with no need to peel","i