erdam Forcing - Amfine'","entityDescription":"An annual, deciduous vegetable, and one of the earliest carrot varieties which can be grown under cloches or in a greenhouse as an extra early crop. It is sweet flavoured carrot with a crunchy texture and orange-red blunt cylindrical roots. Also suitable to grow in containers. Sow March – May, harvest May – August.","image":"","commonName":"carrot 'Amsterdam Forcing - Amfine'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":246937,"botanicalName":"<em>Daucus</em> <em>carota</em> 'Amsterdam Forcing 3'","entityDescription":"As the name suggests this variety is ideal for forcing by sowing early in the season under frames or cloches. Harvested as ‘finger’ carrots they are very sweet and have virtually no core. They are fast to mature and produce uniform cylindrical baby carrots with a good orange colour.  Also suitable for growing in containers or small gardens. Sow from January/ February (if under cover), March if not, through until July. Harvest April – October.","image":"TS012716.jpg","commonName":"carrot 'Amsterdaum Forcing 3'","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":342102,"botanicalName":"<em>Daucus</em> <em>carota</em> 'Artemis'","entityDescription":"A deep orange, Nantes type carrot with a lot to offer due to its superb taste, good resistance to bolting and its nearly year-round harvest season. Carrots can be pulled as baby carrots in the early summer but can stand over winter with a bit of straw protection. This cultivar also has some resistance to spot and scab.  Sow March to July; harvest July through the winter (with some protection)","image":"","commonName":"carrot 'Artemis'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":307220,"botanicalName":"<em>Daucus</em> <em>carota</em> 'Atomic Red'","entityDescription":"A tapered carrot which reaches 25cm long. It has green feathery leaves and a distinctly red root which is retained when cooked","image":"grjo02473.jpg","commonName":"carrot 'Atomic Red'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":119325,"botanicalName":"<em>Daucus</em> <em>carota</em> 'Autumn King 2'","entityDescription":"A handsome, richly orange-coloured maincrop carrot which has stood the test of time and is an allotment favourite for its reliability and excellent flavour. The roots are long, tapering and sturdy, and store well: they can be left in the ground through winter or lifted and packed into boxes of damp sand, where they'll stay good as new for months.  Sow April to June, harvest from August.","image":"","commonName":"carrot 'Autumn King 2'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":107428,"botanicalName":"<em>Daucus</em> <em>carota</em> 'Bangor'","entityDescription":"This variety is said by some to be one of the best maincrops for a gardener. It produces high yields of large, cylindrical roots with a lovely colour and excellent flavour. It also resists cracking, is resistant to greening and stores well after harvesting.  A great all-rounder.  Sow February to July, harvest June until December.","image":"visi120725.jpg","commonName":"carrot 'Bangor'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":534869,"botanicalName":"<em>Daucus</em> <em>carota</em> 'Black Nebula'","entityDescription":"An annual, deciduous vegetable to around 30cm in height, and the darkest coloured variety available.  It produces long, tapering black-purple roots which retain their colour even when cooked, with a crunchy texture and earthy flavour.  Perfect steamed, raw in salads or even as an ingredient for a healthy, dark purple smoothie.  Sow end of March to June, harvest August to November","image":"","commonName":"carrot 'Black Nebula'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":343709,"botanicalName":"<em>Daucus</em> <em>carota</em> 'Burpees Short N Sweet'","entityDescription":"An annual, deciduous vegetable to around 25cm in height, producing 10cm long bright orange roots with a crisp and sweet flavour.  Sow outdoors from March to June for harvesting from June to November.  An ideal variety for pots and containers or for heavier soils where other varieties may struggle","image":"","commonName":"carrot 'Short N Sweet'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":343703,"botanicalName":"<em>Daucus</em> <em>carota</em> 'Cascade'","entityDescription":"A fast-growing stump-rooted carrot reaching around 15cm long. It has green feathery leaves and very uniform, sweet-tasting orange roots","image":"visi120724.jpg","commonName":"carrot 'Cascade'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":199438,"botanicalName":"<em>Daucus</em> <em>carota</em> 'Chantenay Red Cored'","entityDescription":"An annual vegetable with a blunt end and feathery green leaves which are very ornamental.","image":"","commonName":"carrot 'Chantenay Red Cored'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":307222,"botanicalName":"<em>Daucus</em> <em>carota</em> 'Cosmic Purple'","entityDescription":"'Cosmic Purple' is a plant usually grown as an annual for its edible taproot. This cultivar produces tapering roots up to 18cm long with purple skins and bright orange cores","image":"Web_Use-PUB0036198_13952.jpg","commonName":"carrot 'Cosmic Purple'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":342106,"botanicalName":"<em>Daucus</em> <em>carota</em> 'Deep Purple'","entityDescription":"An annual vegetable with a  long, slender habit and purple colour, with feathery green leaves which are very ornamental.","image":"visi120715.jpg","commonName":"carrot 'Deep Purple'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":246943,"botanicalName":"<em>Daucus</em> <em>carota</em> 'Early Nantes 2'","entityDescription":"An annual vegetable with a blunt end and feathery green leaves which are very ornamental.","image":"","commonName":"carrot 'Early Nantes 2'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":241838,"botanicalName":"<em>Daucus</em> <em>carota</em> 'Eskimo'","entityDescription":"An annual, deciduous vegetable and a superb F1 variety that is suited to both early and late sowings. It produces rich orange roots with a sweet flavour, and has strong tops that make it easy to harvest. Shows a good resistance to disease as well as a high tolerance to frost, meaning the carrots can be left in the ground and lifted as required throughout the winter, without losing flavour. Sow April to July, harvest June to January","image":"TS012695.jpg","commonName":"carrot 'Eskimo'","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":343705,"botanicalName"